{
    "background_story": "Keith was a British soldier who fought in the Battle of Omdurman in 1898. Stationed in the Sudan, he was part of the forces led by General Herbert Kitchener that clashed with the Mahdist army. Keith's bravery in the face of overwhelming odds earned him a reputation among his comrades. During the battle, he single-handedly took down several enemy positions, allowing his unit to advance. After the battle, Keith was commended for his valor and received a medal for his service. Though the experience left him shaken, Keith remained proud of his role in the battle and the sacrifices he made for his country. He returned to England a hero, but the memories of Omdurman stayed with him forever, a reminder of the harsh realities of war.",
